o the development of several preventio; 10%; changes in gut microbiota is an important part of elucidating the mechanism of action; increase with polyphenol consumption [16]; changes in gut microbiota; 0.24%; 0.54%; 30 kg/m; 25%; 32%","Nutrition & Metabolism (2024) 21:83 https://doi.org/10.1186/s12986-024-00851-7 RESEARCH Effect of Sinetrol® Xpur on metabolic health and adiposity by interactions with gut microbiota: a randomized, open label, dose– response clinical trial Jananee Muralidharan1, Cindy Romain1, Linda Chung2, Pedro Alcaraz2, Francisco Javier Martínez‑Noguera2, Mayoura Keophiph || Methods In this open label study, we evaluated the effect of Sinetrol® Xpur supplementation on healthy but over‑ weight/obese adults (20–50 yrs) for 16 weeks. || Results We observed HDL, HbA1C, LDL and leptin improved significantly over 16 weeks, irrespective of the dosage. || Conclusions Overall chronic supplementation of Sinetrol® Xpur, irrespective of their dose improved HDL, HbA1c, LDL and leptin and tended to decrease visceral adipose tissue via changes in gut microbiota. || Keywords Obesity, Polyphenols, Gut microbiota, Fat loss, Metabolism Open Access © The Author(s) 2024. || Fla - vanones such as naringenin and hesperidin have shown glucose lowering and lipid modulating effects in invitro studies, however the human studies have shown incon - sistent results [10, 11].","Muralidharan et al. Nutrition & Metabolism (2024) 21:83 https://doi.org/10.1186/s12986-024-00851-7 RESEARCH Effect of Sinetrol® Xpur on metabolic health and adiposity by interactions with gut microbiota: a randomized, open label, dose– response clinical trial Jananee Muralidharan1, Cindy Romain1, Linda Chung2, Pedro Alcaraz2, Francisco Javier Martínez‑Noguera2, Mayoura Keophiphath3, Benjamin Lelouvier4, Patricia Ancel5, Benedicte Gaborit5 and Julien Cases1* Abstract Background Sinetrol ® Xpur is a polyphenolic ingredient rich in citrus flavonoids that has shown weight loss effects in previous studies. The