PMID:31987116,PubMed,31987116,"Effect of a low energy diet, containing a high protein, probiotic condensed yogurt, on biochemical and anthropometric measurements among women with overweight/obesity: A randomised controlled trial.",weight,"Within-group comparisons revealed significant reductions in systolic blood pressure (P = 0.035) and weight (P = 0.005) in the intervention group.; Long-term consumption of Kashk, as a high protein and calcium product enriched with probiotic that is accompanied by a low energy diet, might have beneficial effects on anthropometric and biochemical indices, though more cross-over and parallel blinded trials with placebo groups are needed to confirm these results.",P = 0.013; P = 0.049; P = 0.018; P = 0.037; P = 0.047; P = 0.035; P = 0.005,,,,,,,,detail_hint,expansion2_queue,pending,,"Effect of a low energy diet, containing a high protein, probiotic condensed yogurt, on biochemical and anthropometric measuremen(科研通-ablesci.com).pdf",1.000,7,probiotic condensed yogurt; yogurt; probiotic enriched product; probiotic that is accompanied by a low energy diet; probiotic contents; probiotic food and sup- plements on anthropometric and biochemical parameters among indiv; probiotic consumption on obesity reported that modulation of gut microbiota by probiotic; yogurt for a long time,8 weeks; 3 months,"- viation; CFU, colony forming u; unites (CFU)/g of L. acidophi; .79 /C2 106 CFU/g of B. lactis Bb; La5 (CFU/g) 1.85 /C2 10 6; Bb12 (CFU/g) 1.79 /C2 106 E",70 women,glucose; triglycerides; cholesterol; body mass index; waist circumference; BMI; HDL; LDL; insulin; microbiota; body weight; body fat,"Original article Effect of a low energy diet, containing a high protein, probiotic condensed yogurt, on biochemical and anthropometric measurements among women with overweight/obesity: A randomised controlled trial Elham Razmpoosh a, b, Saeideh Zare b, Hossein Fallahzadeh c, Sara Sa ﬁ a, b, Azadeh Nadjarzadeh a, b, * a Nutrition and Food Security Research Center, Shahid Sadoughi University of Medical Sciences, Yazd, Iran b Department of Nutrition, Faculty of Health, Shahid Sadoughi University of Medical Sciences, Yazd, Iran c Department of Biostatistics and Epidemiology, Faculty of Health, Shahid Sadoughi University of Medical Sciences, Yazd, Iran article info Article history: Received 16 July 2018 Accepted 2 October 2019 Keywords: Dairy product Obesity Anthropometry Blood pressure Blood glucose Lipids summary Background & aims: The aim of this study was to determine the effect of low en",,,106 CFU; 10 8 CFU,8 weeks; 3 months; 5 days; 24 weeks; 6 months,70 women; n=80; n=70; n=35; n=3; n=1; n=6; n=4; n=32; n=33,randomised; controlled trial; parallel; clinical trial; randomized; crossover; placebo controlled; double-blind,diet; yogurt; milk,P < 0.05; P < 0.01,"decreased triglycerides (P ¼ 0; changes as well as psychological and social supports [2]; reduced negative outcomes and therefore are better solutions for weight management; increase in the faecal fat excretion [ 5,6]; increases dietary-induced thermogenesis and satiety compared to diets of lower protein c; 25 kg/m; 95%; 80%; 15%; increased to 35; 50 kcal; 60%; 6%; 3%; 12%; 500 kcal; 27%; 58%","Original article Effect of a low energy diet, containing a high protein, probiotic condensed yogurt, on biochemical and anthropometric measurements among women with overweight/obesity: A randomised controlled trial Elham Razmpoosh a, b, Saeideh Zare b, Hossein Fallahzadeh c, Sara Sa ﬁ a, b, Azadeh Nadjarzadeh a, b, * a Nutrition and Food Security Research Ce || Methods: 70 women with overweight/obesity were randomly assigned to receive either a low energy diet contained 50 g of Kashk (intervention group) or a low energy diet without Kashk (control group) for 8 weeks. || Results: Between-group comparisons showed that the intervention group signi ﬁcantly decreased triglycerides (P ¼ 0.013) and low density lipoprotein cholesterol ( P ¼ 0.049) levels relative to the control 